  {
   "n": 8,
   "topic": "Arithmetic series",
   "spec_refs": [
    "MM2.2"
   ],
   "difficulty": 3,
   "stem_html": "<p>The sum of the first 20 terms of an arithmetic series is 610, and the sum of the first 10 terms is 155.</p><p>What is the 15th term?</p>",
   "diagram_svg": null,
   "options": {
    "A": "32",
    "B": "41",
    "C": "50",
    "D": "47",
    "E": "44"
   },
   "answer": "E",
   "solution_html": "<p>10(2<span class=\"math\">a</span> + 19<span class=\"math\">d</span>) = 610 and 5(2<span class=\"math\">a</span> + 9<span class=\"math\">d</span>) = 155, so 2<span class=\"math\">a</span> + 19<span class=\"math\">d</span> = 61 and 2<span class=\"math\">a</span> + 9<span class=\"math\">d</span> = 31. Subtract: 10<span class=\"math\">d</span> = 30, <span class=\"math\">d</span> = 3, <span class=\"math\">a</span> = 2.</p><p>15th term = 2 + 14 \u00d7 3 = <span class=\"key\">44</span>.</p>",
   "traps": {
    "A": "a + 10d, the 11th term.",
    "B": "a + 13d, the 14th term.",
    "C": "Uses d = 3, a = 5 from an arithmetic slip.",
    "D": "a + 15d, the 16th term."
   }
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "topic": "Geometric series",
   "spec_refs": [
    "MM2.3"
   ],
   "difficulty": 3,
   "stem_html": "<p>A convergent geometric series has sum to infinity equal to 3 times its first term.</p><p>The odd-numbered terms (1st, 3rd, 5th, \u2026) form another geometric series. The sum to infinity of this new series, as a fraction of the sum to infinity of the original series, is</p>",
   "diagram_svg": null,
   "options": {
    "A": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>1</span><span>3</span></span>",
    "B": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>3</span><span>5</span></span>",
    "C": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>1</span><span>2</span></span>",
    "D": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>2</span><span>3</span></span>",
    "E": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>9</span><span>5</span></span>"
   },
   "answer": "B",
   "solution_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">a</span>/(1 \u2212 <span class=\"math\">r</span>) = 3<span class=\"math\">a</span> gives <span class=\"math\">r</span> = 2/3.</p><p>Odd-numbered terms: first term <span class=\"math\">a</span>, ratio <span class=\"math\">r</span><sup>2</sup> = 4/9, sum <span class=\"math\">a</span>/(1 \u2212 4/9) = 9<span class=\"math\">a</span>/5.</p><p>Fraction = (9<span class=\"math\">a</span>/5) / (3<span class=\"math\">a</span>) = <span class=\"key\">3/5</span>.</p>",
   "traps": {
    "A": "1/3 is 1 \u2212 r, not the required ratio.",
    "C": "Assumes the odd terms are exactly half the total; they are more than half because they start first.",
    "D": "2/3 is the common ratio.",
    "E": "9/5 is the odd-term sum divided by a, not by the original sum."
   }
  },
  {
