   "options": {
    "A": "7",
    "B": "5<span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">2</span></span>",
    "C": "14",
    "D": "10",
    "E": "7<span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">2</span></span>"
   },
   "answer": "E",
   "solution_html": "<p>The angle at (0, 0) is a right angle, so (6, 0) to (0, 8) is a diameter: centre (3, 4), radius 5.</p><p>Distance from (3, 4) to <span class=\"math\">x</span> \u2212 <span class=\"math\">y</span> = 0 is |3 \u2212 4|/<span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">2</span></span> = 1/<span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">2</span></span>.</p><p>Half-chord = <span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">25 \u2212 \u00bd</span></span> = <span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">49/2</span></span> = 7/<span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">2</span></span>, so chord = <span class=\"key\">7<span class=\"rt\">\u221a<span class=\"ov\">2</span></span></span>.</p>",
   "traps": {
    "A": "The half-chord's numerator; forgot the \u221a2 and the doubling.",
    "B": "Half the correct chord, roughly.",
    "C": "Doubled the diameter.",
    "D": "The diameter; the line y = x does not pass through the centre."
   }
  },
  {
